From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no growth campaigns (Google's promotions)

ChromeOS's growth framework shows Google's in-product promotions: nudges
and notifications from campaigns in the growth-campaigns DLC, which only
Google's update servers serve. On NickelOS every session asked dlcservice
for that DLC in vain (14 times in the release check of 16852.17.4), each
failure leaving a dlc_service_failure crash report, and it has nothing to
show anyway. kGrowthFramework is off by default: the campaigns manager
isn't started, in sessions or in demo mode (both checks go through
IsGrowthFrameworkEnabled).

---
diff --git a/ash/constants/ash_features.cc b/ash/constants/ash_features.cc
index ee982f8..280a031 100644
--- a/ash/constants/ash_features.cc
+++ b/ash/constants/ash_features.cc
@@ -815,7 +815,11 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kFeatureManagementGrowthFramework,
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Enables growth framework.
-BASE_FEATURE(kGrowthFramework, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// NickelOS: off. It shows Google's promotions (campaigns from the
+// growth-campaigns DLC, which only Google's update servers have: on NickelOS
+// every session asked dlcservice for it in vain, each time leaving a crash
+// report).
+BASE_FEATURE(kGrowthFramework, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Enable set app window as nudge parent.
 BASE_FEATURE(kGrowthCampaignsNudgeParentToAppWindow,
